:{"agent_clan":"sase-16e","agent_clan_generation":"20260922121455","approve":true,"bead_id":"sase-16e.1","changespec_name":"gh_sase-org__sase","cl_name":"gh_sase-org__sase","clan_summary":"[bold #D75FFF]◆ EPIC sase-16e[/bold #D75FFF]\n[dim]  Title: [bold #D7AFFF][/dim]Self-healing agent workspace preparation[/bold #D7AFFF]\n[dim]   Goal: [#D7D7AF][/dim]A new SASE agent launch into a numbered ephemeral workspace never [/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]         [#D7D7AF][/dim]fails because of state an earlier run left behind (unpublishable [/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]         [#D7D7AF][/dim]sidecar commits, merge/rebase conflicts, in-progress git [/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]         [#D7D7AF][/dim]operations, dirty or diverged checkouts). Old state is rescued [/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]         [#D7D7AF][/dim]durably outside the workspace on a best-effort basis, the workspace[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]         [#D7D7AF][/dim]is healed or re-created from the primary checkout, and the [/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]         [#D7D7AF][/dim]bead-merge bug that triggered the original failure is fixed at its [/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]         [#D7D7AF][/dim]root.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim] Counts: [bold #D7AFFF][/dim]6[dim][/bold #D7AFFF] phases[dim][/dim] · [bold #D7AFFF][/dim]3[dim][/bold #D7AFFF] waves[/dim]\n[dim]   Path: [#87AFFF][/dim]plan:202609/[bold #87AFFF][/#87AFFF]self_healing_workspace_prep.md[/bold #87AFFF]\n[dim]  1 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Durable rescue store and non-refusing sidecar eviction[/bold #D7AFFF]        [bold black on #FFD75F] medium [/bold black on #FFD75F]\n    [#AF87FF]rescue-store[dim] · [dim][/dim]no dependencies[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]rescue-store: add a best-effort rescue store outside the workspace (git [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]bundles, worktree patches, manifests, retention, one notification per [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]rescue) and change launch-time sidecar protection to publish once, [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]rescue, and always proceed with eviction instead of raising [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]_WorkspaceBeadEvictionRefused.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  2 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Self-healing checkout preparation for numbered workspaces[/bold #D7AFFF]     [bold black on #FFD75F] medium [/bold black on #FFD75F]\n    [#AF87FF]checkout-heal[dim] · [dim][/dim]after rescue-store[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]checkout-heal: give prepare_workspace an opt-in self-heal ladder for [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]numbered workspaces that rescues state, aborts in-progress git [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]operations, survives stash failures, replaces a conflicting sync rebase [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]with rescue plus hard reset to the default branch, and verifies a clean [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]postcondition.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  3 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Last-resort workspace re-creation and non-holding setup [/bold #D7AFFF]      [bold black on #FFD75F] medium [/bold black on #FFD75F]\n      [bold #D7AFFF]failures[/bold #D7AFFF]\n    [#AF87FF]reclone[dim] · [dim][/dim]after checkout-heal[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]reclone: when in-place healing still fails, rescue and move the numbered[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]checkout aside, re-materialize it from the primary checkout, chdir into [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]it, and prepare it once more (launch, retry, and linked-repo paths); [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]release rather than hold workspaces whose setup ultimately failed.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  4 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Order-preserving bead event stream merge in sase-core[/bold #D7AFFF]         [bold black on #FFD75F] medium [/bold black on #FFD75F]\n    [#AF87FF]core-merge[dim] · [dim][/dim]no dependencies[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]core-merge: in the sase-core repo, stop the bead event-stream merge from[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]re-sorting already-published upstream events by timestamp, and accept [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]pure-reorder branches produced by the old merge so wedged clones can [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]heal.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  5 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Bead sync rollback and wedged-clone healing[/bold #D7AFFF]                   [bold black on #FFD75F] medium [/bold black on #FFD75F]\n    [#AF87FF]bead-sync[dim] · [dim][/dim]after core-merge[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]bead-sync: bump the sase-core pin, roll a clone back when the [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]post-integration stream guard rejects an integration, abort cleanly on [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]deadline timeouts, and mirror the pure-reorder tolerance in the Python [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]stream-integrity guard.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  6 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Truthful setup-failure reporting[/bold #D7AFFF]                              [bold black on #87D7FF] small  [/bold black on #87D7FF]\n    [#AF87FF]visibility[dim] · [dim][/dim]no dependencies[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]visibility: make a recorded runner error beat the synthesized \"Runner [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]exited without recording an error\" fallback in the TUI, and make runner [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]stdout line-buffered so the output file interleaves stdout/stderr [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]correctly.[/#D7D7AF]","clan_tribe":"epic","epic_bead_id":"sase-16e","llm_provider":"muse","model":"muse-spark-1.3-contributor","patch_name":"gh_sase-org__sase","phase_bead_id":"sase-16e.1","reasoning_effort":"xhigh","vcs_provider":"GitHub"},"source_run_id":"run-a8f9b13efda44e565a25826f2446c746","started_at":"2026-09-22T16:15:33.534207+00:00","state":"active"},{"capabilities":{"durably_revivable":true,"historically_viewable":true,"missing_requirements":[],"restartable":true},"commits":[],"dismissed_at":null,"files":{"chat":{"digest":"2d450dfd689864b35e842fade7ed28e96e45f70c939314c9c24dd2061a955b9f","path":"agents/bbugyi200.athena.sase-16e.4/chat.md","size_bytes":3534},"commits":{"digest":"ef46a1641df4c3eb0d271eab8062ccb268cd46be2dbc6cbcf4ba6a1baef574e8","path":"agents/bbugyi200.athena.sase-16e.4/commits.json","size_b